@startuml career-switcher
title Bonus use: career-switcher transformation (v2)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFE0B2
  BorderColor #E65100
}

start
:Candidate with substantial experience\nin domain A, wants to move to domain B;

partition "Split the profile in two" {
  :Target-domain (B) skills\n-> treat like a STUDENT: foundation,
   projects, courses, self-study (diagram 09);
  :Prior-domain (A) experience\n-> still genuine PROFESSIONAL maturity;
}

partition "Transferable-skill mapping (the bridge)" {
  :Map domain-A competencies to domain-B equivalents;
  note right
    teacher -> mentoring, structured explanation,
      stakeholder communication, curriculum = product thinking
    analyst -> data rigor, SQL, requirements
    ops manager -> delivery, prioritisation, ownership
  end note
  :Credit meta-skills at PROFESSIONAL level\n(communication, ownership, delivery, domain expertise);
  :Credit target-domain hard skills at FOUNDATION level\n(provenance-discounted, like a student);
}

partition "Hybrid seniority" {
  :seniority = "junior in domain B,
   but a mature professional";
  :potentialScore boosted by proven ability
   to learn & deliver in a prior career;
}

:Scoring profile = "career_switcher"\n(skills/foundation + transferable + potential + motivation);
:Reasoning emphasises the BRIDGE NARRATIVE\n"why domain-A strengths de-risk the switch,
 what must be learned, realistic ramp time";

:Recruiter card: SWITCHER badge,
 prior-domain strengths + target-domain gaps,
 honest ramp-up expectation;

note right
  Reuses the student machinery (foundation skills, potential,
  entry-eligible JD lens) but ADDS a transferable-skill mapper
  and keeps professional credit for meta-skills — the key
  difference from a true beginner.
end note
stop
@enduml
